<DocLayout title="Foundations" description="The concepts behind Farn — how the system thinks before you build with it">
  <h1>Foundations</h1>
  <p>
    Foundations is the concept layer. It explains <em>how Farn thinks</em> — the ideas and
    rationale behind the system — before you reach for specific token values. For the concrete
    values you look up while building, see <a href="/styles">Styles</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What lives here</h2>
  <p>These pages are being built out as part of the site restructure:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Surfaces</strong> — the theme + depth model (<code>data-theme</code> and <code>data-surface</code>), why it works the way it does, and how it aligns with the palette. <span class="badge badge-draft">Coming soon</span></li>
    <li><strong>Layout</strong> — content-first widths, page structure, and grid-vs-flex guidance. <span class="badge badge-draft">Coming soon</span></li>
    <li><strong>Responsive</strong> — reflow by content rather than device, and fluid typography. <span class="badge badge-draft">Coming soon</span></li>
    <li><strong>Accessibility</strong> — Farn's WCAG&nbsp;AA commitment, focus styles, and reduced-motion approach. <span class="badge badge-draft">Coming soon</span></li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    In the meantime, the surface and theming model is documented on the
    <a href="/tokens/theming">Theming</a> page, and contrast data lives on
    <a href="/tokens/colors">Colors</a>.
  </p>
</DocLayout>
